course: dictionary
lesson: 7482
title: One word, many meanings: positive
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. «I'm positive the bus leaves at nine» means I'm completely sure. Positive here does not mean good or happy. Try your meaning in the sentence: «I'm completely sure the bus leaves at nine» still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: «Think positive, and you might have a better day.» Here positive means hopeful and cheerful, expecting good things to happen. The clues are think and better day. Ask yourself what the writer wants you to feel.
explain: Subjects also change the meaning. In maths, a positive number is above zero, so 5 is positive and minus 5 is negative. In science, a battery has a positive (+) end and a negative (−) end. Same word, different subject: look at the topic and the clues around it.
fact: Positive can mean sure, hopeful, good or useful, a number above zero, or one of the two kinds of electric charge.
fact: «I'm positive» means «I'm completely sure».
fact: In maths, a positive number is greater than zero, so it sits above 0 on a number line.
fact: «A reward given straight after an action makes that action more likely»; this is called positive reinforcement, and it works with dogs, horses, dolphins and even fish.
fact: A battery has a positive (+) end and a negative (−) end.
exercise: «I'm positive the bus leaves at nine.» What does positive mean here? | A number above zero | Very tired | *Completely sure | Cheerful and hopeful about the day
exercise: In maths, what is a positive number? | *Greater than zero | A number with a minus sign | Zero itself | Smaller than zero
exercise: «Think positive, and you might have a better day.» Find and copy the word that means hopeful and cheerful. | *positive | better | day | might
test: In «A reward given straight after an action makes that action more likely», what is positive reinforcement? | Ignoring a dog until it stops | *Rewarding an action straight after it happens, so it is more likely to happen again | Feeding a dog once a week | Punishing a pet for every mistake
test: A battery has two ends. What is the end marked + called? | Neutral | Zero | Negative | *Positive
exam: Which meaning of positive fits «The new bus lanes were a positive change for the town»? | Sure | Above zero | Electric charge | *Good or useful
